  "worked_solution": "The denominators are $3$ and $4.$ We can make a common denominator of $12.$ \n\nWe split the shape on the left of the division sign into $3$ parts vertically, and we split the shape on the right into $4$ parts horizontally:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14155061/assets/1e7a163bb4ee9efb6574e55a37ddeeac3503f2b2b873ba7ba253a969c92d3bb7.png)\n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{12}÷\\frac{8}{12}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n9÷8=1\\,\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}÷\\frac{2}{3}=1\\,\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$",
